# Line endings for the shell files this plugin ships.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE THE REPO-ROOT ONE DOES NOT TRAVEL. The marketplace
# publishes this directory as a `git-subdir` source, and a consuming repo's
# checkout is governed by ITS OWN attributes, not by the source repo's root
# `.gitattributes`. A defect that only manifests downstream is invisible to every
# check run here, so the pin has to live inside the published tree.
#
# What it prevents: `hooks/hooks.json` sources `hooks/probe-python.sh` in every
# wiring. Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its system config, so a
# Windows clone gets CRLF by default unless told otherwise. Shells disagree about
# CR — measured here, Cygwin/Git Bash and its POSIX mode both strip it and the
# probe works, while dash syntax-errors on it — so the failure is a portability
# hazard whose symptom varies by shell rather than one predictable break. Pinned
# rather than characterised.
#
# `hooks/git/pre-push` is the same story for a different reason: every clone
# copies it into `.git/hooks/`, and git refuses to execute a `#!/bin/sh\r`.
hooks/*.sh      text eol=lf
hooks/git/pre-push text eol=lf
